          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em 2-group
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} vertical categorification
            of the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          %p
            It is the special case of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-group"} n-group
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            which is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated"} 1-truncated
            = succeed "-equivalence," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected"} connected
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-type"} homotopy 2-types
          %p
            Somewhat more precisely, a
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              \-group
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+groupoid"} monoidal groupoid
            in which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            with any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            has an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
            up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            = succeed "-equivalence," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            with a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
            of objects.
          %p
            Like other notions of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %h3#strict_groups
            Strict
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %p
            The earliest version studied is that of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
          %p
            A
            %strong
              strict
              = succeed "-group" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            consists of:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a collection of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                homomorphisms of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo ,
                          %mi t
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C_1 \stackrel{s,t}{\to} C_0 \stackrel{i}{\to} C_1
              %p
                such that the composites
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\cdot i
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\cdot i
                are the identity morphisms on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo ,
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1 \times_{t,s} C_1
                for the pullback,
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 1
                              %msub
                                %mo ×
                                %mrow
                                  %mi t
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi s
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mi t
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi s
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      C_1 \times_{t,s} C_1 &amp;\to&amp; C_1
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{t}
                      \\\
                      C_1 &amp;\stackrel{s}{\to}&amp; C_0
                      }
              %p there is, in addition, a homomorphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo ,
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi comp
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C_1 \times_{t,s} C_1 \stackrel{comp}{\to} C_1
              %p
                “respecting
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                and
                = succeed "\u201D;" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %li
              %p
                such that the
                %em composition
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi comp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} comp
                is associative and unital with respect to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                “in the obvious way”.
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
            for further discussion and examples.
          %h3#weak_groups
            Weak
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %p
            A
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                weak
                = succeed "-group" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                \-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            where every morphism is invertible and
            = succeed ":" do
              %em such that
          %ul
            %li
              given any object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
