          %h2#References References
          %h3#OriginalArticles Original articles
          %p The notion of 2-groups first appears in
          %ul
            %li#Solian72
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandru+Solian"}> Alexandru Solian
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Groupe dans une catégorie
                %strong 275
                (1972) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k57310477/f7.item"}> ark:/12148/bpt6k57310477/f7
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Solian80
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandru+Solian"}> Alexandru Solian
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Coherence in categorical groups
                %strong 9
                10 (1980) 1039-1057 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1080/00927878108822631"}> doi:10.1080/00927878108822631
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p and in
          %ul
            %li#Sinh73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%C3%A0ng+Xu%C3%A2n+S%C3%ADnh"}> Hoàng Xuân Sính
              ,
              = succeed "-cat\u00E9gories," do
                %em Gr
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://pnp.mathematik.uni-stuttgart.de/lexmath/kuenzer/sinh.html"} web
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://pnp.mathematik.uni-stuttgart.de/lexmath/kuenzer/sinh_I.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Sinh_Gr-Categories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Sinh73"} Sinh (1973)
            was supervised by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"} Alexander Grothendieck
            and showed that 2-groups are classified, up to equivalence, by quadruples consisting of:
          %ul
            %li
              a group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %li
              an abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              an action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              as automorphisms of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              an element of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3(G,A)
              = succeed "." do
                %em Sinh invariant
          %p She later published two papers on the subject:
          %ul
            %li#Sinh78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%C3%A0ng+Xu%C3%A2n+S%C3%ADnh"}> Hoàng Xuân Sính
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gr-catégories strictes
                %strong 3
                2 (1978) 47-59 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://pnp.mathematik.uni-stuttgart.de/lexmath/kuenzer/sinh.html"}> web
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://pnp.mathematik.uni-stuttgart.de/lexmath/kuenzer/Hoang_Xuan_Sinh_Gr_categories_strictes.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Sinh83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%C3%A0ng+Xu%C3%A2n+S%C3%ADnh"}> Hoàng Xuân Sính
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Catégories de Picard restreintes
                %strong 7
                1 (1983) 117-122 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://pnp.mathematik.uni-stuttgart.de/lexmath/kuenzer/Hoang_Xuan_Sinh_Categories_de_Picard_restreintes.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://pnp.mathematik.uni-stuttgart.de/lexmath/kuenzer/sinh.html"} web
          %p
            %a{:href => "Sinh78"} Sinh 1978
            appears to prove that every 2-group is equivalent to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
            arising from a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+2-group"} symmetric 2-group
            (i.e. a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            with all objects and morphisms invertible) a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+category"} Picard category
            %em restrained
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{x,x} \colon x \otimes x \to x \otimes x
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity
            for all objects
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of abelian groups.
          %p
            Computational enumeration of geometrically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
            2-groups using the computer program
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "http://pages.bangor.ac.uk/~mas023/chda/xmod/xmod244.html"} XMod
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Murat Alp, Christopher Wensley,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Enumeration of
                    = succeed "-groups" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi Cat
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat^1
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.worldscientific.com/doi/abs/10.1142/S0218196700000170"} doi:10.1142/S0218196700000170
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graham+Ellis"}> Graham Ellis
                , Luyen Van Le,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy 2-types of Low order
                %strong 23
                4 (2014) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1080/10586458.2014.912059"}> doi:10.1080/10586458.2014.912059
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://hamilton.nuigalway.ie/preprints/2t.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#review Review
          %p
            An early textbook account on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-groups"} strict 2-groups
            and explaining the relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+modules"} crossed modules
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
              , §XII.8 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
              %strong 5
              Springer (second ed. 1997) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"}> doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Exposition of general 2-groups as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            with all objects and morphisms invertible (sometimes called
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+2-groups"} Picard 2-groups
          %ul
            %li#BaezLauda03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Lauda"} Aaron Lauda
              = succeed "," do
                %em HDA V: 2-Groups
              %strong 12
              14 (2004) 423-491 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.QA/0307200"}> arXiv:math.QA/0307200
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/12/14/12-14abs.html"} tac:12-14
          %h3#geometric_2groups Geometric 2-groups
          %p
            Beware that most of the above discussion is about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+infinity-group"} geometrically discrete
            2-groups.
          %p
            Discussion of geometrically structured 2-groups (notably
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+2-groups"} smooth 2-groups
          %ul
            %li#Schommer-Pries11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"}> Chris Schommer-Pries
              ,
              %em Central Extensions of Smooth 2-Groups and a Finite-Dimensional String 2-Group
              Geometry &amp; Topology
              %strong 15
              (2011) 609-676 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.2483"}> arXiv:0911.2483
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/gt.2011.15.609"} doi:10.2140/gt.2011.15.609
          %p
            and via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+stacks"} group stacks
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              , §2.6.5 &amp; §3.4.2 of:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.7930"}> arXiv:1310.7930
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            For more on this see the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
          %h3#examples_2 Examples
          %p
            A key example due to its universality for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+central+extensions"} higher central extensions
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-group"} circle 2-group
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+2-groups"} smooth 2-groups
            is
          %ul
            %li
              the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
              – see
              %a{:href => "string+2-group#References"} there
              for references.
          %p
            Further on
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+central+extensions"} extensions
            by the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-group"} circle 2-group
          %p
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tori"} tori
            (see also at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality+2-group"} T-duality 2-group
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nora+Ganter"}> Nora Ganter
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categorical Tori
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.7046"} arXiv:1406.7046
